            "review_title": "Review at Kim's Hideaway",
            "review_text": "Piet B\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam28 contributions\n0\nOld-style European atmosphere\nJun 2016 • Friends\nTucked away in Japan Town, off Le Thanh Ton and Thai Van Lung, is this indeed real Hide Away Cafe.... It's 'normally' peaceful and homey. As if you were in house's living-room, except for the fact you can order a drink here. This place is a colonial remnant and has as such preserved the feel, look at the ceiling and you'll know. Highly recommended if you want to sit peacefully with a drink. And Gil is always playing good popular music from a historical play-list, American and European\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 17, 2016",
